comment26.params=docks
comment26.target=void setDocks(java.util.ArrayList)
comment26.text=\r\n Replace the collection of docks visited by the bike.\r\n @param docks New list of visited docks.\r\n
comment27.params=arrivalStep
comment27.target=void setArrivalStep(int)
comment27.text=\r\n Change the arrival step of the bike to its final destination.\r\n @param arrivalStep New arrival step (-1 if it has not arrived yet).\r\n
comment28.target=void calculateRoute()
comment28.text=\r\n Calculates the optimal route for the bike.\r\n If there is enough battery to reach the target, it changes the rechargingLocation to null.\r\n If there isn't enough battery to reach the target, it attempts to find an intermediate \r\n {@link BikeStation} and sets it as the {@code rechargingLocation}.\r\n
comment29.target=java.lang.String getStringRoute()
comment29.text=\r\n Gets a string representation of the planned route, including the recharging stop if one exists.\r\n @return A string showing the route\: {@code currentLocation -> [rechargingLocation ->] targetLocation}.\r\n
comment3.target=int getBatteryLevel()
comment3.text=\r\n Returns the current battery level of the bike.\r\n @return The current battery level.\r\n
comment30.params=endLocation
comment30.target=boolean enoughBattery(Location)
comment30.text=\r\n Checks whether the current battery level is sufficient to reach a given {@link Location}.\r\n The bike consumes {@code EBCompany.MOVINGCOST}ws per step so it could travel up to {@code batteryLevel / EBCompany.MOVINGCOST} steps.\r\n @param endLocation, The {@link Location} checked as destiny.\r\n @return {@code true} if the destiny is reachable and {@code false} otherwise.\r\n
comment31.target=int distanceToTheTargetLocation()
comment31.text=\r\n Get the Manhattan-like distance to the final target location from the current location.\r\n @return The distance to the target location.\r\n
comment32.target=Dock recharge()
comment32.text=\r\n Simulates the recharging process when the bike arrives at its\r\n {@code rechargingLocation}.\r\n\r\n <p>  If the station has a free {@link Dock}, the bike occupies it, the battery\r\n      is charged to full capacity, the cost is calculated, and the station is\r\n      marked as visited. If there is no free dock, the method returns without\r\n      making any change.</p>\r\n\r\n <p>  On a successful recharge, {@code wsCharged}, {@code idleCount},\r\n      {@code chargesCount} and {@code chargesCost} are updated accordingly.</p>\r\n
comment33.target=void reduceBatteryLevel()
comment33.text=\r\n Reduces the battery level by the cost of one movement step (defined in {@link EBCompany\#MOVINGCOST}).\r\n
comment34.params=step
comment34.target=void act(int)
comment34.text=\r\n Carries out a single step of the bike's actions.\r\n Moves one step towards the target (recharging or final) or stays idle.\r\n \r\n <p> If no recharge is needed, it notifies \r\n     when approaching the target destination and moves forward. <p>\r\n <p> If a recharge is needed, checks if it can recharge and show when it does,\r\n     if it is far from the station, moves, if possible, one step closer.<p>\r\n \r\n Finally, it prints the bike's current status to the console.\r\n\r\n @param step The current step of the simulation.\r\n
comment35.target=java.lang.String toString()
comment35.text=\r\n Returns a detailed string representation of the electric bike.\r\n @return The bike's state as \r\n {@code (ElectricBike\: <id>, <cap>wh, <level>wh, <charges>, <cost>\u20AC, <idle>, <loc>[, <rechargeLoc>], <target>)}.\r\n
comment4.target=int getWsCharged()
comment4.text=\r\n Returns the total battery recharged in this bike (ws)\r\n @return The total of ws recharged in this bike.\r\n
comment5.target=int getChargesCount()
comment5.text=\r\n Returns the amount of recharges done by this bike.\r\n @return The amount of recharges done by the bike.\r\n
comment6.target=java.util.ArrayList getDocks()
comment6.text=\r\n Returns the collection of docks visited by the bike.\r\n @return The docks visited by the bike.\r\n
comment7.target=java.lang.String getIdBike()
comment7.text=\r\n Returns the id of the bike\r\n @return The id of the electric bike.\r\n
comment8.target=Location getLocation()
comment8.text=\r\n Returns the bike actual location.\r\n @return The current bike location.\r\n
comment9.target=Location getTargetLocation()
comment9.text=\r\n Returns the destiny location of the bike.\r\n @return Where this bike is ultimately headed.\r\n
